BT /F2 19 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 747 Tm (DBOps Operator Guide) Tj ET
0.35 0.41 0.50 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 726 Tm (Daily operations, backup, recovery, and safe administration) Tj ET
0.11 0.30 0.72 rg
BT /F2 11.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 702.3 Tm (Purpose and operating model) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 688.1 Tm (DBOps is a self-hosted control plane for registering database targets, monitoring health, operating PostgreSQL) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 676.4 Tm (snapshots, and managing remote database hosts. Select and verify the target before any action. Dashboard monitoring) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 664.7 Tm (is separate from changes made directly in an external database.) Tj ET
0.11 0.30 0.72 rg
BT /F2 11.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 646 Tm (1. Sign in and orient yourself) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 631.8 Tm (Sign in with your assigned account. If MFA is enabled, complete the Microsoft Authenticator step. At first sign-in) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 620.1 Tm (after a password reset, enter the temporary password as Current password and choose a different new password of at) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 608.4 Tm (least 12 characters.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 596.7 Tm (Console manages targets and servers; Overview shows health and performance; Backups handles snapshots; Restore) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 585 Tm (Center and Restored DBs handle recovery; Data Browser is read-only; Activity records recent operator actions.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 573.3 Tm (The active-target selector changes the database used by monitoring and relevant actions. Confirm its name before) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 561.6 Tm (pinging, browsing, taking a snapshot, or starting a restore. Backup schedules select their own source database.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 549.9 Tm (Refresh reloads metrics. Live refresh can be paused. The theme toggle changes appearance. Ctrl+K \(Command+K on Mac\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 538.2 Tm (opens the command palette.) Tj ET
0.11 0.30 0.72 rg
BT /F2 11.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 519.5 Tm (2. Register and manage database targets) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 505.3 Tm (Choose Add database instance in Console and enter a clear display name, engine, and connection details. Registration) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 493.6 Tm (stores a connection record; it does not copy, create, or migrate the database. Test connectivity before relying on) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 481.9 Tm (monitoring. Use the narrowest database permissions practical.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 470.2 Tm (Supported engines are PostgreSQL, MongoDB, MySQL/MariaDB, and Redis. Metric coverage differs by engine and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 458.5 Tm (permissions. Snapshots, archive verification, and restore currently support PostgreSQL only.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 446.8 Tm (Changing a display name changes only its DBOps label. Unregistering removes only the app record. Treat full) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 435.1 Tm (connection URLs as credentials.) Tj ET
0.11 0.30 0.72 rg
BT /F2 11.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 416.4 Tm (3. Read the dashboard and inspect data) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 402.2 Tm (Overview presents connectivity and available signals such as connections, database size, cache ratios, slow queries,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 390.5 Tm (deadlocks, and recognized migration history. Missing data can reflect engine limits, permissions, or connectivity. A) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 378.8 Tm (green dashboard is not a substitute for database monitoring.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 367.1 Tm (Migration History reads recognized PostgreSQL migration ledger tables. It reports records; it never applies or) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 355.4 Tm (reverses migrations.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 343.7 Tm (Data Browser performs read-only inspection and returns at most 200 rows per request.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 332 Tm (Ping checks connectivity. Kill cancels a running query and can disrupt an application. Confirm the target and query) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 320.3 Tm (before using it.) Tj ET
0.4 0.46 0.56 rg
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 28 Tm (DBOps Operator Guide | Page 1 of 3) Tj ET
