0.09 0.13 0.20 rg
BT /F2 16 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 734.3 Tm (Backup and recovery workflows) Tj ET
0.11 0.30 0.72 rg
BT /F2 11.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 709.3 Tm (4. Create and verify PostgreSQL snapshots) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 695.1 Tm (Open Backups and choose Take Snapshot. Confirm the PostgreSQL target, archive format, compression, optional) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 683.4 Tm (encryption, and description. Manual snapshots are stored locally. Select remote servers for additional copies. Wait) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 671.7 Tm (for completion and review copy-verification details.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 660 Tm (Custom archive is recommended for flexible pg_restore recovery. Plain SQL is useful for script-oriented workflows.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 648.3 Tm (Encrypted archives require the configured key; losing or changing it can make them unreadable.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 636.6 Tm (Verify checks archive integrity but does not test application recovery. Download retrieves a local archive. Deleting) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 624.9 Tm (the local snapshot removes only its local archive and entry; remote copies remain.) Tj ET
0.11 0.30 0.72 rg
BT /F2 11.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 606.2 Tm (5. Configure an automated schedule) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 592 Tm (Open Backup Schedule, choose the PostgreSQL source, select daily, weekly, or monthly, enter Sri Lanka local time,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 580.3 Tm (and set Active. The editor converts the time to UTC and shows both zones for the next run. Default: daily at 07:30) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 568.6 Tm (Sri Lanka time \(02:00 UTC\). Weekly schedules use the selected Sri Lankan weekday. Monthly schedules allow days 128.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 556.9 Tm (Every scheduled snapshot is first stored locally. Selected mounted repositories and remote servers receive) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 545.2 Tm (checksum-verified copies. The schedule source is independent of the active dashboard target.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 533.5 Tm (After saving, review source, status, destinations, and next run. Keep a loaded custom schedule only if it remains) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 521.8 Tm (intended. Disabled pauses future runs.) Tj ET
0.11 0.30 0.72 rg
BT /F2 11.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 503.1 Tm (6. Restore safely) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 488.9 Tm (In Restore Center, select a completed snapshot and inspect source, timestamp, format, and available local or) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 477.2 Tm (verified remote copy. Choose a registered PostgreSQL destination. Prefer a new, unused database name to protect the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 465.5 Tm (original. Remote copies support new-database restores only.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 453.8 Tm (A new-database restore requires the exact phrase RESTORE. Writing into an existing database requires RESTORE) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 442.1 Tm (EXISTING and writes snapshot objects and data into that database. This can disrupt workloads or replace data; verify) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 430.4 Tm (source and destination before confirming.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 418.7 Tm (Follow job status and logs to completion. Snapshot exports omit owner and privilege settings; configure roles,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 407 Tm (grants, and ownership separately when required.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 395.3 Tm (Restored DBs lists clone restores. Add to Targets registers one for monitoring. Remove from Targets unregisters it) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 383.6 Tm (but does not delete its database.) Tj ET
0.11 0.30 0.72 rg
BT /F2 11.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 364.9 Tm (7. Recovery readiness) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 350.7 Tm (Check that scheduled snapshots complete, remote copies show checksum verification, and storage capacity is) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 339 Tm (sufficient. Default local retention is 14 days. Back up encryption keys separately from encrypted archives.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 327.3 Tm (Periodically restore into a disposable database and confirm the application can use it.) Tj ET
0.4 0.46 0.56 rg
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 28 Tm (DBOps Operator Guide | Page 2 of 3) Tj ET
