BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 750 Tm (DBOps Operator Guide) Tj ET
0.09 0.13 0.20 rg
BT /F2 16 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 734.3 Tm (Remote infrastructure, administration, and response) Tj ET
0.11 0.30 0.72 rg
BT /F2 11.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 709.3 Tm (8. Register servers and provision containers) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 695.1 Tm (Register a remote Linux Docker server with a display name, SSH-reachable host, port, account, and permitted) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 683.4 Tm (database/snapshot paths. Inspect its SSH fingerprint, compare it with a trusted provider or server source, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 671.7 Tm (confirm verification. Use absolute Linux paths whose parent directories already exist. SSH credentials are encrypted) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 660 Tm (in the app registry.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 648.3 Tm (Server health and managed-container panels report connectivity, resources, and DBOps-created containers. Renaming) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 636.6 Tm (changes only the app label. Removing registration does not stop containers or delete files.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 624.9 Tm (Provisioning requests engine, DBOps label, unique container name, database name/user \(except Redis\), password of) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 613.2 Tm (16128 characters, supported image, and host port. Review the connection URL and destination before creating.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 601.5 Tm (The app checks that the host port is free, then checks again before creation. This is a point-in-time check; Docker) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 589.8 Tm (final bind is authoritative. New containers and data directories are created under configured paths; existing) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 578.1 Tm (containers are not changed.) Tj ET
0.11 0.30 0.72 rg
BT /F2 11.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 559.4 Tm (9. Storage, notifications, and alerts) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 545.2 Tm (Mounted storage targets provide repository destinations. Registered remote servers provide SSH copy destinations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 533.5 Tm (Confirm copies are completed and checksum-verified before relying on them for recovery.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 521.8 Tm (Alerts can use thresholds for connection saturation, cache efficiency, slow queries, and migration-ledger changes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 510.1 Tm (Telegram, email, and webhook channels may be configured; test delivery and protect tokens and recipient details.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 498.4 Tm (Alerts are investigation signals, not proof of impact or a completed fix.) Tj ET
0.11 0.30 0.72 rg
BT /F2 11.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 479.7 Tm (10. Users and access) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 465.5 Tm (Administrators create accounts with the correct role and optional MFA. If MFA is enabled, securely deliver the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 453.8 Tm (individual QR code or setup key. Password resets sign the user out and require a new password at next sign-in; MFA) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 442.1 Tm (remains enabled. Admin has additional account-management authority. Avoid shared accounts.) Tj ET
0.11 0.30 0.72 rg
BT /F2 11.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 423.4 Tm (11. Operational safety and troubleshooting) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 409.2 Tm (Connection failure: verify active target, host and port, credentials, network route, firewall, and database) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 397.5 Tm (permissions; then test again.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 385.8 Tm (SSH or provisioning failure: verify host reachability and fingerprint, SSH/Docker access, absolute paths, supported) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 374.1 Tm (image, unique container name, password limits, and port. Verify host-key changes with a trusted source; never bypass) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 362.4 Tm (host-key checking.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 350.7 Tm (Snapshot or restore failure: record the job ID and redacted error, check disk space and destination permissions,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 339 Tm (confirm encryption key, and ensure a new database name is unused. Do not retry an existing-database restore until) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 327.3 Tm (its impact is understood.) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 315.6 Tm (Use Activity to correlate actions and timestamps. Never share passwords, API keys, full connection URLs, MFA setup) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 303.9 Tm (codes, private keys, or unredacted logs.) Tj ET
0.11 0.30 0.72 rg
BT /F2 11.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 285.2 Tm (12. What DBOps does not do) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 271 Tm (DBOps is an operations interface, not a managed database service. Registration does not guarantee credentials are) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 259.3 Tm (read-only. Migration history does not roll migrations back. Ping does not certify health, and archive verification) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 247.6 Tm (does not prove application recovery. Removing a registration does not delete underlying data. Maintain independent) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 235.9 Tm (access controls, monitoring, backups, and tested recovery procedures.) Tj ET
0.11 0.30 0.72 rg
BT /F2 11.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 217.2 Tm (Operator closeout) Tj ET
0.15 0.20 0.29 rg
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 203 Tm (Before ending a maintenance window, record the target and operator, confirm snapshot and copy status, capture) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 191.3 Tm (restore outcomes, review alerts and Activity, and communicate unresolved failures through the approved incident) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 46 179.6 Tm (process.) Tj ET
